print("4. Query x = 2^i for i in 0..63? Each query gives low byte of T^{2^i}(seed) = JUMPS[i](seed) low 8 bits.")
print("   Actually state_at(2^i, seed) = JUMPS[i](seed) (since only bit i set). And JUMPS[i] = T^{2^i}.")
print("   We get 8 bits per query. 8 queries (i=0..7) give 64 equations on seed's 64 bits. Solve.")
print("5. Solve GF(2) system for seed.")
print("6. Solve for x with state_at(x,seed) & 0xFFFFFF == target (24 equations, 64 unknowns).")
print("7. Query that x with known plaintext -> keystream -> XOR with flag ciphertext -> flag.")
